  "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{1}{3}$ on the left and $\\frac{2}{3}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129500/assets/0aebc9b26354aefbfc3e0f6a87e95c41280cb3da40729c32f38e6cdafc155686.png)\n\nThe shape on the left has $1$ shaded piece, and the shape on the right has $2$ shaded pieces. So the number of shaded pieces has increased by a factor of $2.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\times 2=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $2.$",
